  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Accelerating Implementation of Economic Recovery Strategy through Results and Accountability</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Kenyan Government realizes that the key capacity enhancement challenge in Kenya today is to implement the country.s PRSP . the Economic Recovery Strategy (ERS).  At the request of the Government, the Bank has support various Ministries in sharpening the results focus of the ERS, defining the results for the next three years, prioritizing the investment program, and using rapid results approach (RRA) to jump-start implementation. The proposed program is intended to help the government accelerate implementation of its ERS through scaling up and institutionalizing the rapid-results approach in its operations.  The grant will support implementation in HIV/AIDS, Water services, Education, &amp; Agriculture.  Other areas might include Public Sector management.  To assist the Recipient in scaling-up and institutionalizing the Rapid Results Approach (RRA) in its economic recovery strategy, through:  (a) orienting senior government officials on RRA and launching a large number of additional Rapid Results Initiatives (RRIs) in a number of ministries; (b) training local RR coaches and champions to strengthen long-term support capacity; and (c) strengthening existing implementation, monitoring and evaluation mechanisms through results-focused indicators and monitoring and evaluation information systems</narrative>
  </description>
